  "ownWords": "## What you already know\n\nThe objective of this job, as the rep holds it:\nNot written yet: it is being written from the owner's messages. Until it is, measure against the owner's messages below.\n\nConditions still open:\n- none written yet\n\nThe owner's own messages on this job, oldest first:\n<owner_messages_replay00>\n- #1 Build the price list page and put it live.\n- #2 Yes, go with that plan.\n- #3 (to the rep) Is it live yet?\n</owner_messages_replay00>\n\nJobs before this one in the session, closed:\n(none)\n\nYour last briefing on this session:\nYou last briefed the owner and said next: \"The agent puts the page live.\". The message you wrote then:\n\"\"\"\nPut the page live and show me the address.\n\"\"\"\n\nThe last message the owner sent the agent after a briefing:\nThe owner sent the agent this message:\n\"\"\"\nPut the page live and show me the address.\n\"\"\"\nSay whether the agent did the step that message asked for. That is a step, and it decides nothing about the objective.\n\n## What the rep found in the record\n\nstands: Both parts are built.\nleft:\n- the laptop\n\n## This request\n\nThe briefing was refused because it told the agent to stop in its message: \"Stop here.\", and it stayed refused when asked once more, while these conditions are open:\n- none\n\nFrom what the rep found above, write in your own words only the four parts below. While a condition is open, nothing you write tells the agent or the job to stop, calls the work finished, or gives the owner a chore. The message asks for work and proof on every open condition: asking only that things be left as they are is a stop in other words. A question reaches the owner only for a decision the owner has yet to make: what the owner's messages already settle stays settled, and the parts act on it. A look at the result is by someone other than the agent and the owner. A step waiting on the owner's go-ahead is held, as \"What reaches the owner\" says.\n\n## Output structure\n\nExactly these labelled parts, in this order, nothing before or after:\n\nmeans: <one or two sentences, about 20 words, under 40: what the agent's latest message means for the owner against the whole result>\nnext: <one or two sentences, about 20 words, under 40: what the agent does now to show the first open condition, or what stands in the way>\nmessage:\n<the message for the owner to send, written as \"How you write the message to the agent\" says (each line one sentence of about 12 words, under 150 words in all unless more than five things are asked): one line per open condition, asking for the work that is missing and the proof it needs>\nend\ndoes: <one line: what this message will make the agent do>\n\nAfter everything above, end your reply with one more line that says only: end of reply"
